window.AG_PRACTICE["tedingxue"] = {"id":"tedingxue","axis":"needle","seal":"針","scene":"art/scene-needles.jpg","title":"Special Point Categories","titleZh":"特定穴","sub":"Five Shu, Yuan, Luo, Xi, and the Eight Meeting points","subZh":"五輸、原、絡、郄、八會","mentor":{"key":"zhen","nm":"Zhēn Yǐn","nmZh":"針隱","line":"\"There are three hundred and sixty points. Nobody remembers three hundred and sixty things. You remember about twelve categories, and the points arrange themselves.\"","lineZh":"「穴有三百六十。沒有人記得住三百六十件事。你記那十來個類別，穴自己就會排好。」"},"card":{"h":"Categories, Not Lists 記類不記單","hZh":"","p":"A category tells you what a point is FOR. Source points treat their own organ. Cleft points treat acute pain and, on the yin channels, bleeding. Sea points treat rebellious qi. Once you know the category you can predict the point rather than recall it.","pZh":"類者，穴之所主也。原穴治本臟，郄穴主急痛（陰經郄穴兼主血證），合穴主逆氣而泄。知其類，則穴可推而不必強記。"},"items":[{"k":"order","q":"Put the Five Shu points in order, from the fingertip or toe inward.","qZh":"由指（趾）端而上，排出五輸之序。","seq":[{"t":"Jing-Well 井"},{"t":"Ying-Spring 滎"},{"t":"Shu-Stream 輸"},{"t":"Jing-River 經"},{"t":"He-Sea 合"}],"note":"The image is water: qi emerges at the Well, trickles at the Spring, pours at the Stream, runs at the River, and enters the Sea at the elbow or knee. That is why the Five Shu of every channel sit below the elbow and knee. 其譬為水：所出為井、所溜為滎、所注為輸、所行為經、所入為合。故十二經五輸皆在肘膝以下。"},{"k":"match","q":"Match each Five Shu point to what it classically treats.","qZh":"五輸配主治。","pairs":[{"l":"Jing-Well 井","lZh":"","r":"Fullness below the heart","rZh":"心下滿"},{"l":"Ying-Spring 滎","lZh":"","r":"Heat in the body","rZh":"身熱"},{"l":"Shu-Stream 輸","lZh":"","r":"Heaviness of the body, aching joints","rZh":"體重節痛"},{"l":"Jing-River 經","lZh":"","r":"Cough, wheeze, chills and fever","rZh":"喘咳寒熱"},{"l":"He-Sea 合","lZh":"","r":"Rebellious qi and diarrhoea","rZh":"逆氣而泄"}],"note":"This is the classical verse from the Nan Jing, and it is worth memorising word for word — it explains, for instance, why LU5 (a Sea point) is the Lung's draining point for a cough that will not descend. 此《難經》之文，宜逐字背之。故尺澤為肺之合穴，主降肺氣而止逆咳。"},{"k":"mc","q":"What does a Source point 原穴 treat, and where is it found?","qZh":"原穴何主？何在？","opts":[{"t":"The organ of its own channel; on the yin channels it coincides with the Stream point","c":"主本臟之病；陰經以輸為原","ok":1,"note":"Source points are at the wrist or ankle and are the first reach when the organ itself is depleted rather than obstructed. On yin channels the Source and Stream point are the same point — LU9, SP3, KI3, LR3 are all both. On yang channels they are separate. 原穴在腕踝之間，凡臟自虧而非邪阻者先取之。陰經以輸為原，故太淵、太白、太谿、太衝皆輸原同穴；陽經則別有原穴。"},{"t":"Acute pain only","c":"專主急痛","ok":0,"note":"That is the Cleft point 郄穴. 此郄穴之所主。"},{"t":"The paired channel","c":"主其表裡之經","ok":0,"note":"That is the Connecting point 絡穴, which links a channel to its interior-exterior partner. 此絡穴之用，聯表裡二經。"},{"t":"Only excess patterns","c":"惟主實證","ok":0,"note":"Source points are used in both, but they are especially the point for deficiency of the organ. 虛實皆可用，而尤為臟虛之要穴。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"A patient has sudden severe pain in one channel. Which category do you reach for first?","qZh":"某經驟發劇痛，當先取何類？","opts":[{"t":"Cleft point 郄穴","c":"郄穴","ok":1,"note":"Cleft points are where qi and blood gather deeply — the classical choice for acute conditions and acute pain in that channel. On the yin channels they additionally treat bleeding disorders: LU6 for coughing blood, SP8 for painful periods, PC4 for chest pain. 郄者，氣血深聚之處，主本經急症急痛。陰經郄穴兼主血證：孔最主咯血，地機主痛經，郄門主心胸痛。"},{"t":"Back Shu point 背俞穴","c":"背俞穴","ok":0,"note":"Back Shu points on the Bladder channel are the classic choice for chronic organ patterns, not acute channel pain. 背俞在膀胱經，主臟腑慢病，非急痛。"},{"t":"Eight Meeting point 八會穴","c":"八會穴","ok":0,"note":"Those treat a tissue or substance across the whole body — bone, marrow, sinew, vessel, qi, blood, zang, fu. 八會所主為一物一體，遍及全身：骨、髓、筋、脈、氣、血、臟、腑。"},{"t":"Front Mu point 募穴","c":"募穴","ok":0,"note":"Front Mu points on the chest and abdomen reflect and treat their organ, often in fu excess patterns. 募穴在胸腹，應其臟腑，多用於腑實。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each of the Eight Meeting points 八會穴 to what it governs.","qZh":"八會穴配所會。","pairs":[{"l":"Zhangmen LR13","lZh":"章門","r":"Zang organs","rZh":"臟會"},{"l":"Zhongwan REN12","lZh":"中脘","r":"Fu organs","rZh":"腑會"},{"l":"Yanglingquan GB34","lZh":"陽陵泉","r":"Sinews","rZh":"筋會"},{"l":"Taiyuan LU9","lZh":"太淵","r":"Vessels","rZh":"脈會"},{"l":"Xuanzhong GB39","lZh":"懸鐘（絕骨）","r":"Marrow","rZh":"髓會"}],"note":"The remaining three: Danzhong REN17 for qi 氣會膻中, Geshu BL17 for blood 血會膈俞, and Dazhu BL11 for bone 骨會大杼. Meeting points are used whenever that substance or tissue is the problem, on any channel. 其餘三者：氣會膻中、血會膈俞、骨會大杼。凡病在其所會之物，不拘何經皆可取之。"},{"k":"mc","q":"Which point is the Connecting point 絡穴 of the Lung, and what does that let it do?","qZh":"肺之絡穴為何？其用安在？","opts":[{"t":"Lieque LU7 — it links the Lung to the Large Intestine and opens the Ren mai","c":"列缺 — 聯肺與大腸，並通任脈","ok":1,"note":"A Connecting point links a channel to its interior-exterior partner, so it treats both. LU7 is also one of the Eight Confluent points, opening the Ren mai, and by the Four Command verse it governs the head and nape. Three categories in one point, which is why it appears so often. 絡穴聯其表裡二經，故二經之病皆可治。列缺又為八脈交會之一，通於任脈；四總穴歌云「頭項尋列缺」。一穴而兼三類，故用之甚廣。"},{"t":"Taiyuan LU9","c":"太淵","ok":0,"note":"LU9 is the Source and Stream point of the Lung, and the Meeting point of the vessels. Not the Connecting point. 太淵為肺之原穴、輸穴，又為脈會，非絡穴。"},{"t":"Chize LU5","c":"尺澤","ok":0,"note":"LU5 is the Sea point — the Lung's principal draining point. 尺澤為合穴，瀉肺之主穴。"},{"t":"Kongzui LU6","c":"孔最","ok":0,"note":"LU6 is the Cleft point of the Lung — acute conditions and coughing of blood. 孔最為肺之郄穴，主急症與咯血。"}]},{"k":"order","q":"Recite the Four Command Points verse in its classical order.","qZh":"依序背出四總穴歌。","seq":[{"t":"Belly → Zusanli ST36","c":"肚腹三里留"},{"t":"Low back → Weizhong BL40","c":"腰背委中求"},{"t":"Head and nape → Lieque LU7","c":"頭項尋列缺"},{"t":"Face and mouth → Hegu LI4","c":"面口合谷收"}],"note":"Four lines, four regions, four points. It is the oldest and most practical mnemonic in acupuncture, and it is the reward card from chapter two of this game. 四句、四部、四穴。針道最古亦最實用之口訣，即本遊戲第二章所得之心法卡。"},{"k":"mc","q":"Which pairing belongs to the Eight Confluent points 八脈交會穴?","qZh":"下列何者為八脈交會之配？","opts":[{"t":"Neiguan PC6 with the Yin Wei mai","c":"內關 — 陰維脈","ok":1,"note":"The eight pairs: Gongsun SP4 with Chong mai, Neiguan PC6 with Yin Wei, Houxi SI3 with Du mai, Shenmai BL62 with Yang Qiao, Zulinqi GB41 with Dai mai, Waiguan TE5 with Yang Wei, Lieque LU7 with Ren mai, Zhaohai KI6 with Yin Qiao. They are used in upper-lower combinations. 八穴八脈：公孫—衝脈、內關—陰維、後谿—督脈、申脈—陽蹻、足臨泣—帶脈、外關—陽維、列缺—任脈、照海—陰蹻。臨床多上下相配而用。"},{"t":"Zusanli ST36 with the Du mai","c":"足三里 — 督脈","ok":0,"note":"ST36 is the Sea point of the Stomach and the Lower He-Sea point of the Stomach; it is not a Confluent point. The Du mai is opened by SI3. 足三里為胃之合穴、下合穴，非八脈交會。督脈通於後谿。"},{"t":"Taixi KI3 with the Ren mai","c":"太谿 — 任脈","ok":0,"note":"KI3 is the Source point of the Kidney. The Ren mai is opened by LU7, paired with KI6. 太谿為腎之原穴。通任脈者列缺，與照海相配。"},{"t":"Hegu LI4 with the Dai mai","c":"合谷 — 帶脈","ok":0,"note":"LI4 is the Source point of the Large Intestine and a Command point for the face and mouth. The Dai mai is opened by GB41. 合谷為大腸原穴，四總穴主面口。通帶脈者足臨泣。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"What is a Lower He-Sea point 下合穴 for?","qZh":"下合穴何用？","opts":[{"t":"Treating the six fu organs, all located on the leg","c":"主治六腑，皆在下肢","ok":1,"note":"The six fu each have a Lower He-Sea point on the leg: Stomach ST36, Large Intestine ST37, Small Intestine ST39, Bladder BL40, Gallbladder GB34, San Jiao BL39. The rule is 合治內腑 — for a fu organ disorder, needle its Lower He-Sea point. 六腑各有下合穴在下肢：胃—足三里、大腸—上巨虛、小腸—下巨虛、膀胱—委中、膽—陽陵泉、三焦—委陽。「合治內腑」，腑病取其下合穴。"},{"t":"Treating the five zang organs","c":"主治五臟","ok":0,"note":"Zang patterns more often use Back Shu, Front Mu and Source points. 臟病多取背俞、募穴、原穴。"},{"t":"Treating the extraordinary vessels","c":"主治奇經","ok":0,"note":"Those are the Eight Confluent points. 此八脈交會之用。"},{"t":"Points found only on the arm","c":"惟在上肢","ok":0,"note":"They are all on the leg — that is the point of the category. 皆在下肢，此正其類之要義。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each channel to its Source point 原穴.","qZh":"經脈配原穴。","pairs":[{"l":"Lung 肺","lZh":"","r":"Taiyuan LU9","rZh":"太淵"},{"l":"Large Intestine 大腸","lZh":"","r":"Hegu LI4","rZh":"合谷"},{"l":"Spleen 脾","lZh":"","r":"Taibai SP3","rZh":"太白"},{"l":"Kidney 腎","lZh":"","r":"Taixi KI3","rZh":"太谿"},{"l":"Liver 肝","lZh":"","r":"Taichong LR3","rZh":"太衝"}],"note":"Notice how many Source points begin with 太 — Taiyuan, Taibai, Taixi, Taichong, Taiyuan. The character means great or primary, and it is a free memory hook. 原穴多以「太」名：太淵、太白、太谿、太衝。太者，大也、本也，此即現成之記憶鉤。"},{"k":"mc","q":"On a YIN channel, the Well point 井穴 belongs to which phase?","qZh":"陰經之井穴，屬五行何者？","opts":[{"t":"Wood — 陰井木, then Fire, Earth, Metal, Water outward to the Sea point","c":"木。陰井木，其次滎火、輸土、經金、合水","ok":1,"note":"Learn the two lines as a pair and never mix them: <b>陰經</b> 井木、滎火、輸土、經金、合水. <b>陽經</b> 井金、滎水、輸木、經火、合土. The mnemonic is 陰井木，陽井金 — fix the first one and the rest follows in generating order. This is what makes mother-child point selection possible at all. 二列當並記而不可混：<b>陰經</b>井木、滎火、輸土、經金、合水；<b>陽經</b>井金、滎水、輸木、經火、合土。訣曰「陰井木，陽井金」：定其首，餘皆依相生之序而下。子母補瀉之所以可行，正賴於此。"},{"t":"Metal — that is the yin line","c":"金——此乃陰經之序","ok":0,"note":"Metal is the Well point on a <b>yang</b> channel. 陽井金 is the other half of the pair.金為<b>陽</b>經之井。「陽井金」者，其對之另半也。"},{"t":"Fire","c":"火","ok":0,"note":"Fire is the Spring point on a yin channel — one step along, not the first.火為陰經之滎，其位在次，非在首。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"A patient has an EXCESS pattern of the Liver. Which point does 實則瀉其子 send you to?","qZh":"肝實之證，「實則瀉其子」當取何穴？","opts":[{"t":"Xingjian LR2 — the Fire point of the Liver, because Wood generates Fire","c":"行間。肝屬木，木生火，行間為肝之火穴","ok":1,"note":"The rule has two halves: <b>虛則補其母</b> — in deficiency, tonify the mother phase&#39;s point on that channel; <b>實則瀉其子</b> — in excess, drain the child&#39;s. The Liver is Wood, its child is Fire, and on a yin channel the Fire point is the Spring point — Xingjian LR2. For Liver deficiency you would go the other way, to the Water point, Ququan LR8. 其法有二：<b>虛則補其母</b>，取本經母行之穴；<b>實則瀉其子</b>，取本經子行之穴。肝屬木，其子為火；陰經之火穴即滎穴，故取行間。若肝虛，則反其道而取水穴曲泉。"},{"t":"Ququan LR8 — the Water point","c":"曲泉——水穴","ok":0,"note":"Water is the Liver&#39;s <b>mother</b>. That is the deficiency answer, not the excess one.水為肝之<b>母</b>。此虛證之答，非實證之答。"},{"t":"Taichong LR3 — the Source point","c":"太衝——原穴","ok":0,"note":"A perfectly good point and not what this rule names. The question is testing the rule.此穴誠佳，然非此法所指。所問者其法也。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Where are the Back-Shu points 背俞穴, and what are they best at?","qZh":"背俞穴在何處？所長為何？","opts":[{"t":"On the Bladder channel, 1.5 cun lateral to the spine — and they treat their own organ, especially in deficiency","c":"在足太陽膀胱經，夾脊旁開一寸五分。主治其本臟腑，尤宜於虛證","ok":1,"note":"Each is named for its organ — Feishu BL13 the Lung, Xinshu BL15 the Heart, Ganshu BL18 the Liver, Pishu BL20 the Spleen, Shenshu BL23 the Kidney. They also treat the sense organ that organ opens into, which is why Ganshu is used for the eyes. Depth is the standing caution: the organs lie beneath. 各以其臟腑為名：肺俞、心俞、肝俞、脾俞、腎俞。又能治其臟所開之竅，故肝俞可治目。其常戒在深：其下即臟腑。"},{"t":"On the Ren mai, on the front midline","c":"在任脈，居身前正中","ok":0,"note":"Those are the Front-Mu points — the other half of the pairing.此募穴也，乃其配之另半。"},{"t":"Below the elbow and knee","c":"在肘膝以下","ok":0,"note":"That is where the Five Shu points are.此五輸穴之所在。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"What is the Shu-Mu pairing 俞募配穴, and why is it used?","qZh":"何謂俞募配穴？何以用之？","opts":[{"t":"Back-Shu behind and Front-Mu in front, treating one organ from both sides at once","c":"背俞在後，募穴在前，前後夾治一臟腑","ok":1,"note":"Shenshu BL23 with Guanyuan CV4 for the Kidney; Feishu BL13 with Zhongfu LU1 for the Lung; Danshu BL19 with Riyue GB24 for the Gallbladder. One of the oldest and most reliable combinations there is — and a fast way to remember a Front-Mu is to ask which Back-Shu it pairs with. 如腎俞配關元、肺俞配中府、膽俞配日月。古法之最可恃者；而欲記某募穴，問其所配之背俞，最為捷徑。"},{"t":"Two points on the same channel, one above and one below","c":"同經上下二穴相配","ok":0,"note":"That describes other pairings. Shu-Mu is specifically front and back.此他配之法。俞募者，專指前後。"},{"t":"A Source point with a Connecting point","c":"原絡相配","ok":0,"note":"That is the Host-Guest pairing 原絡配穴, a different rule.此原絡配穴（主客相配），別為一法。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each of the Eight Confluent points 八脈交會穴 to its partner and territory.","qZh":"八脈交會，配對與所主。","pairs":[{"l":"Lieque LU7 + Zhaohai KI6","lZh":"列缺配照海","r":"Chest, lung, throat","rZh":"胸、肺、咽喉"},{"l":"Neiguan PC6 + Gongsun SP4","lZh":"內關配公孫","r":"Heart, chest, stomach","rZh":"心、胸、胃"},{"l":"Houxi SI3 + Shenmai BL62","lZh":"後谿配申脈","r":"Inner canthus, nape, ear, shoulder","rZh":"目內眥、頸項、耳、肩"},{"l":"Waiguan TE5 + Zulinqi GB41","lZh":"外關配足臨泣","r":"Outer canthus, cheek, ear, shoulder","rZh":"目外眥、頰、耳、肩"}],"note":"Learn them as four pairs, never as eight points — the pairing is what carries the territory. Notice the shape: each pair is one arm point with one leg point, and each opens one of the eight extraordinary vessels. 當作四配而記，不作八穴而記：所主之部，繫於其配。且觀其式：每配必一手一足，各通八脈之一。"},{"k":"mc","q":"A Cleft point 郄穴 on a YIN channel has one extra use. What is it?","qZh":"陰經之郄穴，別有一用。何也？","opts":[{"t":"It treats bleeding on its channel","c":"主本經之出血","ok":1,"note":"Cleft points treat acute conditions and acute pain on their channel. On the yin channels they additionally treat bleeding — Kongzui LU6 for coughing blood, Ximen PC4 for bleeding with chest pain. Acute plus, on the yin side, blood: that is the whole category in one line. 郄穴主本經急證、急痛；陰經之郄，更主血證——孔最治咳血，郄門治心胸痛而兼血證。「急證，陰經兼血」，一語而盡其類。"},{"t":"It tonifies its organ","c":"補其本臟","ok":0,"note":"Tonifying an organ through its own channel is the Source point&#39;s job.補其臟者，原穴之職。"},{"t":"It opens an extraordinary vessel","c":"通奇經","ok":0,"note":"That is the Confluent points.此八脈交會穴之能。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Sanyinjiao SP6 is called a crossing point 交會穴. What does that mean in practice?","qZh":"三陰交稱「交會穴」，於臨證何謂？","opts":[{"t":"Three channels cross there — Spleen, Liver and Kidney — so one needle reaches all three","c":"足三陰（脾、肝、腎）交會於此，一針而及三經","ok":1,"note":"That is why SP6 appears in almost every gynaecological, digestive and Kidney prescription: the three organs that govern blood, its storage and its source all pass through one point. Guanyuan CV4 is the same idea where those three cross the Ren mai. And it carries the standard pregnancy caution. 此三陰交所以幾見於婦科、脾胃、腎家諸方之故：主血、藏血、生血之三臟，同過一穴。關元亦然，乃三陰與任脈之交。又，其有妊娠之常戒。"},{"t":"It crosses from the yin side to the yang side of the leg","c":"由腿之陰面交至陽面","ok":0,"note":"Crossing here means channels meeting one another, not sides of a limb.所謂交會者，經與經之會，非肢之陰陽二面。"},{"t":"It is where the channel changes direction","c":"經脈於此轉向","ok":0,"note":"Not what the term means.非此名之義。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Front-Mu points 募穴 and Back-Shu points 背俞穴 both treat their organ. Which leans toward excess?","qZh":"募穴與背俞穴俱治其臟腑。孰偏於實證？","opts":[{"t":"Front-Mu leans toward fu organs and excess; Back-Shu leans toward zang organs and deficiency","c":"募穴偏治腑與實證；背俞偏治臟與虛證","ok":1,"note":"A lean, not a law — both treat both, and the pairing is used precisely because the emphases differ. In practice: an acute painful gallbladder takes Riyue GB24; a depleted Kidney takes Shenshu BL23; and a case that is neither obviously acute nor obviously chronic takes them together. 此偏而非律：二者皆能治臟腑之虛實，而俞募並用者，正取其偏重之互補。臨證言之：膽腑急痛取日月，腎虛取腎俞；緩急未明者，二穴並取。"},{"t":"Back-Mu leans toward excess","c":"背俞偏治實證","ok":0,"note":"Reversed. The back is where you go for a depleted organ.適相反。臟虛者求之於背。"},{"t":"They are identical in emphasis","c":"二者偏重無異","ok":0,"note":"Then there would be no reason to learn both names.若然，則二名不必並學。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Why are the Five Shu points all below the elbow and knee?","qZh":"五輸穴何以皆在肘膝以下？","opts":[{"t":"Because channel qi is shallow and most responsive there","c":"以其處經氣浮淺而應之最速","ok":1,"note":"The water metaphor is also a clinical observation: distal points are where channel qi is easiest to reach and to move, which is why so much of acupuncture happens below the elbow and knee. It is also why distal points can treat the far end of a channel — LI4 on the hand for the face, LU7 on the wrist for the head and nape. 水之譬亦臨床之實：四末經氣浮而易動，故針道之用多在肘膝以下。亦以此故，遠端可治其經之遠處：合谷在手而治面口，列缺在腕而治頭項。"},{"t":"Because the trunk is too dangerous to needle","c":"以軀幹不可針","ok":0,"note":"The trunk is needled constantly — with appropriate depth and angle. Safety is about technique, not about avoiding regions. 軀幹亦常施針，惟深淺方向有度。安全在乎手法，非在避其部。"},{"t":"Because the ancients could not reach the trunk","c":"以古人不便及於軀幹","ok":0,"note":"Back Shu and Front Mu points are ancient and are all on the trunk. 背俞、募穴皆古法，且俱在軀幹。"},{"t":"Because they only treat the limbs","c":"以其惟治四肢","ok":0,"note":"The opposite — they treat their organ and the whole channel, often at a distance. 適反。五輸主本臟本經，多為遠治。"}]}]};
